    "title": "Beyond the Badge: The Real Origin of the Word \"Cop\"",
    "chineseTitle": "美劇必備單字：「Cop」這個詞是怎麼來的？",
    "passage": "If you watch American movies or crime dramas, you may notice that instead of using \"police officer,\" people prefer the catchy term \"cop.\" Where did this word stem from, and why has it stuck for so long?\n\nOne popular theory is that cop stands for Constable on Patrol. Others believe it comes from copper, since early police officers wore badges made of copper. Both explanations sound convincing, but linguists reject them as myths with no solid historical backing.\n\nMost language authorities trace the term back to the French verb caper, ultimately derived from the Latin capere, meaning \"to seize.\" In the early 1700s, the verb \"cop,\" meaning to catch or to arrest someone, entered English slang. Later, because anyone who \"copped\" others was called a copper, the noun form emerged. By the mid-19th century, copper was shortened to cop in street language.\n\nFrom the early 20th century, cop truly took off through various media, including crime novels and Hollywood films. The word sounds punchy and natural in dialogue, which makes it fit fast-paced storytelling. However, police officer remains the formal term used in legal and professional contexts. Although cop has been regarded as acceptable by most officers today, it may still sound disrespectful depending on tone and meaning. Next time a character on screen shouts \"Cops!\" you'll know exactly what that word has been through.",
    "chineseTranslation": "如果你看美國電影或犯罪影集，可能會注意到大家不說「police officer（警察）」，而偏好用朗朗上口的「cop」。這個字是從哪裡來的？又為什麼能流傳這麼久？\n\n一種流行的說法是，cop 是 Constable on Patrol（巡邏警員）的縮寫。也有人認為它來自 copper（銅），因為早期警察配戴銅製的徽章。這兩種解釋聽起來都很有說服力，但語言學家認為它們都是缺乏可靠史料根據的迷思。\n\n大多數語言權威把這個詞追溯到法文動詞 caper，最早源自拉丁文 capere，意思是「抓住」。在1700年代初期，意指抓住或逮捕某人的動詞「cop」進入了英文俚語。後來，因為「cop」別人的人被稱為 copper，名詞形式便出現了。到了19世紀中葉，copper 在街頭用語中被縮短成 cop。\n\n從20世紀初開始，cop 透過犯罪小說和好萊塢電影等各種媒體真正流行起來。這個字在對白中聽起來有力又自然，很適合節奏明快的故事。不過，police officer 仍是法律和專業場合使用的正式用語。雖然如今大多數警察都能接受 cop 這個稱呼，但依語氣和含意不同，它仍可能聽起來不尊重。下次螢幕上的角色大喊「Cops!（警察來了！）」時，你就會知道這個字經歷了什麼。",
